{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CffxiHYyhJoS8sEHgkNEL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The candidate passed the self-check (`OK`). It refines the incumbent `tally_span_switch_ideal_periodic_unit` as **`graded_near_periodicity_tally_switch`**, and its short test fit gave an ELPD-LOO of −3429.5. The incumbent's full fit scores −3435.5. The test fit was one chain of 100 draws, so that comparison is only a rough hint.\n\n**The one change:** the incumbent penalises a sequence only if it repeats a short unit exactly. The new model makes that penalty graded. For each sequence it takes the best period of two flips or more and measures the share of flips that match the flip one period back. The penalty grows with the square of that share. So a sequence that almost repeats a motif, with one slip (e.g. HHTHHTHT), also looks designed. The tally-span, ideal-switching-rate and left/right-lean parts are unchanged from the incumbent.\n\n**Why this change:** the critique's one flagged problem was that people's choices on individual pairs are more lopsided than the model predicts (p = 0.05, but it does not survive the FDR, q = 0.29). An exact-periodicity switch can't separate near-periodic sequences from irregular ones. In a quick logistic regression on the current responses, the graded cue fit about 35 nats better than the binary one.\n\n**Not yet checked:**\n- **Convergence:** with a single chain, the self-check can't report R-hat.\n- **ELPD reliability:** the LOO estimate was flagged unreliable, with 10.8% of trials over the Pareto-k limit. That may be because the test fit was so short.\n- **Novelty:** this is the main risk. In the same regression, the triplet-variety cue fit about 25 nats better than the graded cue, and the live model `tally_span_switch_ideal_triplet_variety` (tied with the incumbent) already uses it. The new model could be rejected if its predictions come too close to that one's. Still, the graded cue added about 14 nats on top of triplet variety, so the two capture partly different things.\n\nFiles are in `experiment3/model_loop/iter_0/candidate_3/`:\n- hypothesis.md\n- model_name.txt\n- candidate.py"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3692,"cache_read_input_tokens":79018,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3692,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"790f7cac-5b05-40da-97e7-5daf51bbaba8","uuid":"13ff02b6-3ae9-494b-b971-281d980b1d06","timestamp":"2026-10-03T20:48:43.538Z","request_id":"req_011CffxiH7RoFsG2Kaxm9x3P"}
